+ * in the next frame (by its vertex and index addresses, format, count and
+ * how many times the frame drew them), transforms the same vertices with the
+ * previous frame's matrices too, and hands the backend, during its draw()
+ * call, the draw as it is halfway between the two frames, clipped on its own:
+ * psp_render_between_v/n/prim (v NULL: the draw is the same in both, as 2D
+ * is). flip() is called once a frame, at present, with the GE idle. */
